  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-22, in his own words:\n\n> if we look at the lead in and lead out.. the between levels happens at clearance plane.. and between passes happens at retract plane. but i cannot see a retract plane\n\n## What happens\n\nThe Lead in / Lead out tab of a 2D Offset operation has two link rows:\n- \"Between levels\" is set to \"Clearance plane\".\n- \"Between passes\" is set to \"Retract plane\".\n\nThe Heights tab has no Retract Z row. Its Levels group has only \"Hop below clearance\" (off) and \"Stepdown\". The viewport labels three planes: Clearance (32.00, stock top +10), Top (22.00) and Bottom (1.50). It labels no retract plane. So the user cannot see or edit the plane that \"Between passes\" says it uses.\n\n## What the code says\n\n- The hint of the Heights tab says: \"the retract plane: on, links hop at Retract Z; off, every link climbs to Clearance Z\" (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/heights_page.rs`). The Retract Z row exists only while \"Hop below clearance\" is on.\n- The Lead tab lists \"Clearance plane / Retract plane / Keep down\" for each link (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/lead_page.rs`). It does not say which height \"Retract plane\" means when the hop is off.\n- The user guide says that a kind that has one gets a retract plane 10 above the stock top (`operations-2d.md`).\n\n## Not known yet\n\nWhich height the generator uses for a link set to \"Retract plane\" when \"Hop below clearance\" is off, for 2D Offset. The hint of the Heights tab suggests the clearance height. The Lead tab suggests a separate plane. The worker reads the generator and says which one is true.\n\n## Expected\n\nOne of these, and the maintainer chooses:\n- \"Retract plane\" is shown on the Heights tab and in the viewport whenever a link uses it, with its value.\n- Or the choice is hidden or renamed while no retract plane exists.\n\nThe Lead tab then never offers a plane that the user cannot see.\n\n## Related\n\n#3316 is about the same operation (`2D Offset1`, `fig8`, `EM-0800-4FL`). Its warning \"rapid move 543 travels through stock (below the clearance plane, or at it below the stock top)\" asks why three rapids are below the clearance plane. The answer may depend on this link. The worker of #3316 reads this issue.\n\nDone means: a structural UI test shows that the Lead tab and the Heights tab name the same plane, and that the viewport labels it when a link uses it.\n",
